{"title":"2011 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 14","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_2_(Guess_and_Check)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2 (Guess and Check)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_3_(Educated_Guess)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3 (Educated Guess)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_1_by_SpreadTheMathLove\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution 1 by SpreadTheMathLove</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_WhyMath\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by WhyMath</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">8</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_14&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>There are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/9/6/496208bfed993b16f902b0edc179b34b89804160.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$270$\" width=\"26\" height=\"12\" /> students at Colfax Middle School, where the ratio of boys to girls is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/3/843bbcce85c0752818a6573bbc8145a965ceab9b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5 : 4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"35\" height=\"14\" />. There are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/c/b/5cb1b41850ab676e4d1cf15c69b1609af4befbc5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$180$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"26\" height=\"13\" /> students at Winthrop Middle School, where the ratio of boys to girls is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/7/ef7a99fdd3cb1bbec54decf5f73c37509a4d855c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4 : 5$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"32\" height=\"13\" />. The two schools hold a dance and all students from both schools attend. What fraction of the students at the dance are girls?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/8/c/98c940f5f52f0ca1773518b64877316ae8c5dab9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A) } \\dfrac7{18} \\qquad\\textbf{(B) } \\dfrac7{15} \\qquad\\textbf{(C) } \\dfrac{22}{45} \\qquad\\textbf{(D) } \\dfrac12 \\qquad\\textbf{(E) } \\dfrac{23}{45}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"408\" height=\"38\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution\">Video Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_14&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/rQUwNC0gqdg?t=697\">https://youtu.be/rQUwNC0gqdg?t=697</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_14&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>At Colfax Middle School, there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/a/a/baafc5bb419be4a8aca04c41610c86e8737b6075.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac49 \\times 270 = 120$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"113\" height=\"37\" /> girls. At Winthrop Middle School, there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/7/bb74ed058b7f612f8027bbdcb4b5e115da261e00.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac59 \\times 180 = 100$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"113\" height=\"37\" /> girls. The ratio of girls to the total number of students is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/9/5d980053be395d356fdf069d051c4230cf3754f3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{120+100}{270+180} = \\frac{220}{450} = \\boxed{\\textbf{(C)}\\ \\frac{22}{45}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"228\" height=\"48\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_2_.28Guess_and_Check.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2_(Guess_and_Check)\">Solution 2 (Guess and Check)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_14&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2 (Guess and Check)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Since we know there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/9/6/496208bfed993b16f902b0edc179b34b89804160.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$270$\" width=\"26\" height=\"12\" /> kids at Colfax Middle School and we know the ratio of boys to girls is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/0/ad0a4bc0ad5d6415575678e779682fb207069c5b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5:4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"35\" height=\"14\" />, we can use guess and check to find the number of girls at the dance (and vice versa). <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/c/4/3c411c1a5f61fda09f93039e2b176b3778834aee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5:4=150:120$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"129\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/a/17a4194112522c6da7eda9804ac7a3a7aca1b3d7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4:5=80:100$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"120\" height=\"14\" />. Now that the ratios sum to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/9/6/496208bfed993b16f902b0edc179b34b89804160.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$270$\" width=\"26\" height=\"12\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/c/b/5cb1b41850ab676e4d1cf15c69b1609af4befbc5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$180$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"26\" height=\"13\" />, we know that in Colfax there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/a/a/aaa4de95cc6371d125d5cf773cdd9f9913dd1d8e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$120$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"29\" height=\"14\" /> girls and in Winthrop, there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/5/9/e59e2c6e83eb78cca610a5fd4070ae01c8d4ae60.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$100$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"29\" height=\"14\" /> girls. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/3/51350d48d45524b7f10e8ffbde8fa37a86a1876e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$120+100=220$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"130\" height=\"15\" /> total girls and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/1/8/618440abd0fba89481503beb7dd34964d7a6ee88.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$270+180=450$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"130\" height=\"15\" /> total people. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/4/c9414b01b6345973f557454923bc14c5fd865ff5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{220}{450}=\\boxed{\\textbf{(C)} \\frac{22}{45}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -19px\" width=\"119\" height=\"49\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_3_.28Educated_Guess.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3_(Educated_Guess)\">Solution 3 (Educated Guess)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_14&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3 (Educated Guess)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We know that since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/9/6/496208bfed993b16f902b0edc179b34b89804160.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$270$\" width=\"26\" height=\"12\" /> is greater than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/c/b/5cb1b41850ab676e4d1cf15c69b1609af4befbc5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$180$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"26\" height=\"13\" /> and how the ratios are opposites, we know that there will be more boys than girls, so the fraction of students at the dance that are girls should be less than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/f/9/2f960094315d60883495f9b74148e17487ee9584.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"15\" height=\"38\" />. We also know that the amount of girls and the amount of boys are close, so the fraction of students at the dance that are girls should be really close to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/f/9/2f960094315d60883495f9b74148e17487ee9584.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"15\" height=\"38\" />. The only answer choice that/best satisfies these conditions is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/6/3/b63ea5139d20cecf8fc3b82d83d2fb267314665b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(C)}\\ \\frac{22}{45}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -19px\" width=\"69\" height=\"49\" />.\n</p><p>~NXC\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_1_by_SpreadTheMathLove\">Video Solution 1 by SpreadTheMathLove</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_14&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution 1 by SpreadTheMathLove\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=mYn6tNxrWBU\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=mYn6tNxrWBU</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_WhyMath\">Video Solution by WhyMath</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_14&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by WhyMath\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/zAVxg6FmLyk\">https://youtu.be/zAVxg6FmLyk</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_14&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_8\" title=\"2011 AMC 8\">2011 AMC 8</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_8_Problems\" title=\"2011 AMC 8 Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_8_Answer_Key\" title=\"2011 AMC 8 Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Fo